## Commands

- `uv sync` — install/update the environment (uv only; never pip or poetry)
- `uv run pytest` — tests + coverage (floor: {% if adopt %}see pyproject — ratchet toward 85%{% else %}85%{% endif %})
- `uv run ruff check .` then `uv run ruff format .` — lint + format (two commands;
  `&&` breaks in Windows PowerShell 5.1)
- `uv run mypy` — strict type-check

## Rules

- One function, one job. If a docstring needs "and", split the function.
- Modules stay under **500 lines**. Complexity caps (mccabe 10, PLR too-many-*)
  are enforced by ruff, so lint and CI catch them; the 500-line cap is checked
  only by the post-edit gate, per file as you edit it — nothing re-checks it at
  commit or in CI, so code that lands another way (bulk move, merge, hand edit)
  is on you. Decompose instead of suppressing.
- Every function fully typed; mypy runs strict.
- No `print` in library code (ruff T20) — use `logging`.
- New feature = new folder {% if adopt %}in the package{% else %}under `src/{{ package_name }}/`{% endif %}, not new code
  smeared across existing modules.
- Warnings are errors in tests; fix the cause, don't filter.

